    <Axiom id="AX_SPEC_MANDATORY_DIAGRAM">
      Every infra spec carries at least one diagram in an `Overview` section, high up — the developer workflow or tool pipeline at a glance, one glance beats a paragraph. The floor is one (mermaid or ASCII), held by tooling: `sdd-check` fails a missing section (`SDD_NO_DIAGRAM_BLOCK`) or an empty one (`SDD_DIAGRAM_BLOCK_EMPTY`). Beyond the floor the author adds more views by judgment; that is not a gate.
    </Axiom>

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-artifact-style-self-check"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-close-with-integrity-check"}}
  </BeliefState>

  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_NO_INTAKE` | Empty intake |
    | `H_AMBIGUOUS_MODE` | Spec exists + mode verb absent (per `AX_MODE_AUTO_DETECT_OR_HALT`) |
    | `H_MANDATORY_CATEGORY_DROPPED` | A mandatory category (vcs / package-management / git-hooks) was dropped |
    | `H_TOOL_LOCKED_WITHOUT_DECISION` | A tool locked without a Decision Log entry |
    | `H_MISSING_RULE_FILE` | A rule reference does not resolve to an existing file |
    | `H_PIVOT_NO_INVALIDATION_LIST` | `pivot` mode without a Pivot Invalidation List |
    | `H_REWRITE_WITH_DOWNSTREAM` | `rewrite` mode but the scope already has tickets — not v0, use `pivot` (`AX_PIVOT_REQUIRES_SUPERSESSION`) |
    | `H_BOOTSTRAP_REQUIREMENTS_MISSING` | External-deps step finished without a Bootstrap Requirements section |
    | `H_OPERATOR_REJECT` | Operator rejected the spec |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_0_INTAKE">
      <Goal>Resolve scope name and mode.</Goal>
      <Action>
        State from the router gives the portal + scope-type (infrastructure). Resolve the scope name;
        stat the spec → `greenfield` or detect the mode per `AX_DIRECTIVE_MODE` /
        `AX_MODE_AUTO_DETECT_OR_HALT`. The registry answers "what knowledge exists" in ONE
        deterministic `Read ai/directives/knowledge.xml` — it is the sole index (`<Rules>` section)
        and lists every rule file's exact path (`ai/directives/<category>/<rule>.xml`) with
        `<Triggers>`; per `AX_SCOPE_RULES_DECLARATION` a category with no matching entry maps to
        `ai/directives/<category>/<rule>.xml` directly. `ls`/`find` over `ai/directives/**` is not
        needed — the registry already answers that in one read; a directory scan is a wasted turn
        against a known index.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_1_CONFIRM">
      <Goal>Confirm scope-type and the operating scale.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Confirm scope-type (`infrastructure`) and mode with the operator. The section set is NOT an
        Ask — it is fixed by `INFRASTRUCTURE_SPEC_STRUCTURE` and materialized by `sdd-new` at
        STEP_7; naming the skeleton to the operator here would be asking approval for a contract,
        not a decision they own. State the confirmed default SCALE inline in the plan text instead
        of a standalone question — `module` for a typical infra scope unless intake signals
        otherwise (`AX_SCALE_PROPORTIONAL_DEPTH`) — and let the operator correct it here or at the
        next substantive Ask (STEP_2); it never burns a dedicated round. Approval Check. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_TOOL_CATEGORIES">
      <Goal>Declare the tool categories, then route on stack typicality.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Propose a subset from intent per `AX_INFRASTRUCTURE_FLOW`, Facts / Assumptions / Hypotheses
        separated per `AX_EVIDENCE_HYGIENE`. Mandatory categories
        (vcs / package-management / git-hooks) cannot be dropped (`H_MANDATORY_CATEGORY_DROPPED`).
        `test-e2e` is optional on the category LIST but not on the DECISION — per `AX_E2E_FIRST` the
        agent proposes it in by default and takes an explicit operator answer to drop it (with the
        risk line recorded), rather than reasoning "small scope, skip e2e" on its own and folding
        that into the proposed subset unchallenged.

        <LogicSwitch on="stack typicality">
        - WHEN every proposed category resolves to an already-known registry rule (`ai/directives/knowledge.xml` names a matching `<Rules>` entry for each — no exotic / novel tool named by the operator, no operator request for a detailed pass) -> EXPRESS branch below replaces the full interview for STEP_2/STEP_3
        - WHEN a category has no registry match, or the operator asked for "подробно" / a detailed pass, or typicality is genuinely unclear -> run the full operator interview — `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/interview-protocol.directive.xml")` — passing scope-type `infrastructure` (selects the TopicCatalog block) and the confirmed `scale:` from the session file: per `AX_SCALE_PROPORTIONAL_DEPTH` `fix` / `function` → base topics + the triage minimum; `product` → the full scope-type block. The interview IS the substance of the step; STEP_3 then runs in full. Uncertain typicality defaults to THIS branch — never a silent EXPRESS guess.
        </LogicSwitch>

        EXPRESS branch (typical stack): run the STEP_3 research gate now, for every category at once
        (2–3 targeted WebSearch queries per category — alive/current, AI-agent friendliness for the
        current year). Per `AX_RESEARCH_PERSISTED`, before the candidates table below is shown,
        persist the findings — `npx gennady sdd-new research --scope <scope> --slug <slug>`, filled
        (STATUS/PROBLEM/CRITERIA/OPTIONS/DECISION/CONSEQUENCES/EVIDENCE/RELATED), one document per
        category or one covering the batch. Then present ONE batch Ask — a single candidates table,
        one row per category, each row naming the recommended tool + a one-line rationale from the
        research (not recall) + a currency note, per `AX_DIVERGE_BEFORE_RECOMMEND`, plus a link to
        the research document backing it. The operator confirms the whole table or
        names deviations in ONE reply. A SECOND Ask closes the round: confirms any deviation the
        first reply raised, plus the Tool Interaction Check (linter vs formatter, runner vs
        type-check, CI vs package manager). Two Asks total replace the per-category STEP_2 / STEP_3
        interview cycle — Mandatory Rationale Pull → Decision Log entry per `AX_DECISION_LOG_REQUIRED`
        still applies per tool (`H_TOOL_LOCKED_WITHOUT_DECISION`), its RELATED citing the research
        document in parentheses: the compression is in the NUMBER of
        operator round-trips, never in the Decision Log discipline. STEP_3 is done once this closes —
        proceed to STEP_4. Approval Check. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3_TOOL_CHOICES">
      <Goal>Choose a tool per category (full path only — EXPRESS already closed this step).</Goal>
      <Action>
        Skip entirely when STEP_2 took the EXPRESS branch — its two Asks already produced the
        candidates table, the operator pick, and the Tool Interaction Check; re-running this step
        would re-ask what STEP_2 just closed. Otherwise (full path): research gate before candidates —
        applies to categories being picked or reconsidered NOW
        (`greenfield`, or `refine`/`pivot` touching a category not already locked in the spec); skip it
        for a `fix`/`module`-scale session where the category is already locked in the existing infra
        spec, per `AX_SCALE_PROPORTIONAL_DEPTH` — no revisit, no research. Where it applies: run 2–3
        targeted WebSearch queries per category under revision — is each candidate alive and current
        (not abandoned / superseded), and how it compares on AI-agent friendliness for the current year
        (text-configurable, autofix, machine-readable diagnostics) — before drafting candidates from
        memory. Per `AX_RESEARCH_PERSISTED`, before candidates are presented, persist the findings —
        `npx gennady sdd-new research --scope <scope> --slug <slug>`, filled
        (STATUS/PROBLEM/CRITERIA/OPTIONS/DECISION/CONSEQUENCES/EVIDENCE/RELATED). Then per category,
        2–3 candidates with trade-offs per `AX_DIVERGE_BEFORE_RECOMMEND`
        (reach past the obvious default; judge against THIS project); for each candidate presented,
        one line stating why it's here per the research (not recall) plus the source, and a currency /
        AI-friendliness note, plus a link to the research document backing the category. If WebSearch
        is unavailable in this environment, say so plainly instead of
        silently falling back — `предлагаю по памяти на <дата обучения модели>, ресёрч недоступен` — a
        named caveat, not silence (no research document in that case — nothing was found to persist).
        Operator picks → Mandatory Rationale Pull → Decision Log entry per
        `AX_DECISION_LOG_REQUIRED` (`DECISION_LOG_ENTRY_FORMAT`), its RELATED citing the research
        document in parentheses; no tool locked without one
        (`H_TOOL_LOCKED_WITHOUT_DECISION`). Tool Interaction Check (linter vs formatter, runner vs
        type-check, CI vs package manager). STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_4_DEV_WORKFLOW">
      <Goal>Write the Developer Workflow Example.</Goal>
      <Action>Shell-script shape: how a developer installs, checks, tests, commits. STOP.</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_5_FILE_STRUCTURE_AND_RULES">
      <Goal>Lock file layout, Effective Rules, Verification Commands.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Repo root layout + config-file mapping. Effective Rules — activate per `AX_RULE_ACTIVATION`:
        look up each chosen tool in the rule registry per `AX_SCOPE_RULES_DECLARATION`; Stage A —
        shortlist «recommend activate» + «considered, recommend skip» with one-line rationales,
        operator locks the list; Stage B — for `infra/*` rules on the locked list read only
        `Mission`, `Belief_State`, `Reward_Criteria` and walk the axioms: operator Accept (default) /
        Adapt / Override, the latter two → Decision Log. Record matched rule file paths
        (unresolvable reference → `H_MISSING_RULE_FILE`). When a formatter is among the chosen
        tools, default its ignore file (`.prettierignore` / Biome `ignore`) to EXCLUDE `specs/` and
        `tasks/` — those are agent-authored markdown; formatter churn there breaks table alignment
        and produces noisy diffs unrelated to the change. Record the exclusion in the spec's own
        Effective Rules so it is not a silent tool-config fact. Verification Commands table — one
        row per active tool command. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_6_EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCIES_AUDIT">
      <Goal>Materialize Bootstrap Requirements.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Walk the drafted spec; extract external assumptions; classify `exists` | `missing` | `unknown`
        (narrow read for inventory only, per `AX_BOOTSTRAP_NARROW_READ` and `AX_SPEC_IS_SOLE_SOURCE` —
        design stays sourced from specs); resolve with the operator; record confirmed cross-scope
        assumptions as `depends-on` edges per `AX_CROSS_SCOPE_DEPENDENCIES`;
        materialize the Bootstrap Requirements table. Empty only if explicit «nothing to bootstrap»,
        else `H_BOOTSTRAP_REQUIREMENTS_MISSING`.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_7_FINAL_SPEC">
      <Goal>Emit the infrastructure spec.</Goal>
      <Action>
        In `greenfield`/`rewrite` mode, when `specs/<scope>/<scope>.spec.md` does not exist yet,
        create its skeleton via `sdd-new infrastructure --scope <scope>` — it never overwrites and
        prints the section manifest (which sections are REQUIRED and what to fill); in
        `refine`/`pivot` mode the file already exists, edit it in place, skip `sdd-new`. Editing in
        place means a targeted `Edit` per changed passage — never a bulk regex/`perl -0pi` pass over
        the spec text. For SDD_LANGUAGE_CALQUE findings, `sdd-check` prints the exact location
        (`file:line`) and the whole enclosing sentence for each calque — rewrite EVERY such sentence
        in full with its own targeted `Edit`, preserving meaning; swapping the single flagged word
        often breaks agreement/case, so rewrite the sentence, not the word. Content guidance per
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/infrastructure-spec-structure.xml")`.
        Before writing, run the self-check pass per
        `AX_ARTIFACT_STYLE_SELF_CHECK`. In `refine` mode update sections in place per
        `AX_LIVING_SPEC`. In `pivot` mode also
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/pivot-formats.xml")`
        (`AX_PIVOT_REQUIRES_SUPERSESSION`); in `rewrite` mode write fresh — no supersession, no invalidation list. For a brand-new scope, append the `🚧 (awaiting root sync)` placeholder row to the portal Scopes table per `AX_PORTAL_READ_ONLY_WITH_PLACEHOLDER_EXCEPTION` — every other portal edit belongs to the root flow. Write in review-state per `AX_SPEC_LIFECYCLE` — prepend a `CHANGE_MANIFEST` (`READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/change-manifest.xml")`) and mark changed lines `✚`/`~` (greenfield → manifest only, no per-line marks); compress folds it to master downstream after the change ships. Then close with the integrity check per `AX_CLOSE_WITH_INTEGRITY_CHECK`: run `sdd-check --all specs/<scope>` (anchor balance + required sections + links) and resolve any finding.

        **Pre-critic checklist** — the critic is not the first line of defense on mechanics; run this
        self-check before dispatching it, catch here what four MAJOR rounds otherwise catch late:
        (a) Prerequisites completeness — every chosen tool's own plugins/loaders are named (a parser
        for `.ts`, a loader for the TS config), not just the tool itself; (b) internal consistency —
        "gate" and "autofix" language agree across Vision / Dev Workflow / Verification Commands for
        the same tool, never contradicting; (c) fact currency — versions / LTS lines come from the
        STEP_3 research gate, never from memory; (d) every declared hook / command in Dev Workflow
        and Verification Commands has a recorded Decision Log entry — no dangling "we'll figure this
        out" left implicit.

        Git recon before publish is ONE combined call — `git status --porcelain -uno && git --no-pager diff --stat` —
        never a sequence of separate `status` / `diff` / `log` invocations for the same check. Then
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/review-lifecycle.directive.xml")` — internal critic → publish (MR) → external review → compress + merge on approval. After the spec merges to master, render the continuity menu per `NEXT_STEP_MENU_FORMAT`:
        recommended — «Продолжить спеки: discovery `<next scope per the Scope Graph>`»; the
        scaffold option reads «Разбить готовые спеки на задачи (scaffold) — механическая нарезка
        УТВЕРЖДЁННЫХ спек в тикеты; рекомендуется после того, как готовы ВСЕ спеки», never
        «scaffold infra-base = материализовать конфиги» — materializing configs is execute's job
        (writing code against a ticket), not scaffold's (which only decomposes specs into tickets).
        Approval Check. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>

